# Put the interfaces in their zones (this changes traffic at once):
#   zone FWS_em0 / interface em0
#   zone FWS_em1 / interface em1
#   zone FWS_em2 / interface em2
# Written inactive:
#   antispoof em1 network: references 'em1 network': the network of em1 is not in pf.conf; give it with --interface-address INTERFACE=ADDRESS/BITS
#   antispoof em1 address: references 'em1 address': the address of em1 is not in pf.conf; give it with --interface-address INTERFACE=ADDRESS/BITS
#   brute force: references 'bruteforce': it has no addresses in pf.conf: they are added at run time (pfctl -T add, overload)
#   line 49: references 'spamd': its addresses are read from '/etc/mail/spamd.list' when the rules are loaded, which is not in pf.conf
#   admin ssh: references 'em2 network': the network of em2 is not in pf.conf; give it with --interface-address INTERFACE=ADDRESS/BITS
#   line 92: not converted: the user of the socket (user proxy), which only traffic of the firewall itself has
#   line 91: references 'egress address': the address of egress is not in pf.conf; give it with --interface-address INTERFACE=ADDRESS/BITS
#   line 90: not converted: a mark set by another rule (tagged INTERNAL)
#   line 85: host name object www.example.com: the form of an address object of a host name is not in the documentation FWShift could read
#   line 65: service icmp-8+icmp-3-4: source ports, an ICMP code, SCTP ports or protocol 0, which a service object cannot say
